course: dictionary
lesson: 8548
title: Body words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «scalp» may be new to you, but its context gives you clues. Look at the words near it: head, hair, skin, sore, and wash. These all point to one part of the body.
explain: «Pulling hair really hurts, and the scalp can stay sore for days.» Hair is on the scalp, and pulling hair hurts the skin it grows from. So the scalp is the skin on your head where your hair grows.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Pulling hair really hurts, and the skin on your head can stay sore for days.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: The scalp is the skin on the top and back of your head, where your hair grows.
fact: Hair grows from little roots in the scalp.
fact: Head lice live on the scalp, and dandruff is flakes of dry scalp skin.
fact: «A bump on the head swells because the scalp has many blood vessels.» The size of a bump does not show how serious the injury is.
fact: Keep your scalp clean by washing your hair, and protect it from sunburn with a hat.
exercise: «Pulling hair really hurts, and the scalp can stay sore for days.» What is the scalp? | A bone inside your ear | *The skin on the top and back of your head, where your hair grows | The strap of your school bag | A soft pad on your knee
exercise: «A bump on the head swells because the scalp has many blood vessels.» Does a big bump always mean a serious injury? | Only if the bump is purple | *No, the size of a bump does not show how serious the injury is | Yes, a big bump always means a serious injury
exercise: Which is a good way to look after your scalp? | *Wash your hair to keep your scalp clean | Pull your hair hard every morning | Never wash, so dirt can build up | Go out in the midday sun with no hat
test: Dandruff is what? | Little bones of the skull | Tiny bubbles of soap | Hairs that have fallen out | *Flakes of dry scalp skin
test: Where do head lice live? | On the knees | *On the scalp | In the ears | In the stomach
exam: Where do hair roots sit? | In the knee | In the tongue | In the heel | *In the scalp
